---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chaos Daemons Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Chaos Daemons? Learn how Khorne's armies play, how to paint red and brass Khorne daemons, and exactly what to buy first for this melee-aggressive faction."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">👹</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Chaos Daemons</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Pure warp energy given form. Not machines. Not soldiers. Things that should not
            exist, bleeding through the boundary between reality and the immaterium.
            Blood, fire, change, rot, excess — the four gods made manifest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Melee Aggression</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*The Combat Patrol is all Khorne. Other god flavors are equally valid starting points — more on that below.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Chaos Daemons?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Everything that exists in the physical universe has a reflection in the warp — the
          psychic parallel dimension that underlies reality. Every emotion, every thought,
          every act of violence or love or despair sends ripples into the immaterium. Over
          millennia, those ripples coalesced. The strongest emotions, the most powerful and
          repeated impulses of billions upon billions of sentient beings, formed into
          conscious entities of incomprehensible scale.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are four of them. The Chaos Gods. And from each, daemon servants are born
          continuously — fragments of divine will given physical form when the barrier
          between realities thins enough for them to push through. They are not alive in
          any conventional sense. They are <em>ideas</em> made flesh: rage, change, disease,
          desire. They cannot truly be killed, only banished back to the warp to reform.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Khorne</strong> — the Blood God. Red rage, skulls,
          eternal war. His daemons are the simplest and most direct: get close, tear apart,
          offer the skull. They hate sorcery and psychic powers almost as much as they hate
          the enemy. Bloodletters are his foot soldiers. Bloodcrushers ride massive iron
          Juggernauts — daemonic constructs of brass and brute force. Flesh Hounds are
          his hunters, tireless and impossible to outrun.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Tzeentch</strong> — the Changer of Ways. Blue and
          pink, flame and feather, plans within plans. His daemons shift and mutate.
          Horrors split when killed, spawning more. The Lord of Change is a vast
          avian sorcerer of terrible intelligence. The most psychically powerful daemon
          army in the game.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Nurgle</strong> — the Plague Father. Green rot and
          eternal decay, but paradoxically the most joyful of the gods. His Plaguebearers
          shamble forward unstoppably. Nurglings swarm and cling. The Great Unclean One
          is a titanic bloated monstrosity that is almost impossible to kill and
          inexplicably beloved by hobbyists.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Slaanesh</strong> — the Prince of Pleasure. Purple
          and pink, speed and sensation. Daemonettes are razor-quick melee fighters.
          Seekers ride Steeds of Slaanesh at terrifying speed. The Keeper of Secrets is
          an elegant monster of horrifying beauty and lethal precision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          The Combat Patrol is all Khorne — and Khorne plays exactly how it looks.
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">No shooting. No psychic powers</strong> (Khorne despises
          sorcery with a passion). Move forward. Charge. Kill. The strategy is aggression,
          tempo, and getting into combat before the opponent can focus-fire your daemons down.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bloodletters are your core — twenty of them in the Combat Patrol, marching forward
          with Hellblades. Flesh Hounds move faster and are your threat range extenders —
          getting in the opponent's face early to disrupt their plans. Bloodcrushers are
          your heavy hitters: daemon-riders on iron Juggernauts who hit hard enough to
          crush vehicles. The Bloodmaster is your Herald character, buffing nearby units
          and fighting personally in melee.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pure Khorne lists are refreshingly simple to learn: your job is to close distance
          fast and let the melee rules do the work. Beginner-friendly in terms of
          decision-making, though positioning matters enormously for making charges.
          Mixed-god lists — Khorne with Tzeentch or Nurgle support — add significant
          complexity and tactical depth for players who want it later.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- God flavor cards -->
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-4">Pick your god, pick your playstyle</h3>
      <div class="space-y-3 mb-8">
        {[
          {
            god: 'Khorne',
            emoji: '🔴',
            palette: 'Red skin, brass armor, black bases',
            style: 'Aggressive forward melee. No shooting, no magic. Simple and brutal.',
            color: 'text-red-400',
            border: 'border-red-900',
          },
          {
            god: 'Tzeentch',
            emoji: '🔵',
            palette: 'Blue, pink, and purple flames',
            style: 'Psychic firepower, shifting units that multiply when killed. Most complex.',
            color: 'text-blue-400',
            border: 'border-blue-900',
          },
          {
            god: 'Nurgle',
            emoji: '🟢',
            palette: 'Rotting greens and browns',
            style: 'Durable, slow advance. Hard to kill, contagion debuffs on enemies.',
            color: 'text-green-400',
            border: 'border-green-900',
          },
          {
            god: 'Slaanesh',
            emoji: '🟣',
            palette: 'Purple, pink, and bone',
            style: 'Fastest daemons in the game. Devastating charges from range.',
            color: 'text-purple-400',
            border: 'border-purple-900',
          },
        ].map(g => (
          <div class={`bg-[#1a1a1f] border ${g.border} rounded-lg p-4`}>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1">
              <span class="text-xl">{g.emoji}</span>
              <h4 class={`font-display font-semibold ${g.color}`}>{g.god}</h4>
              <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{g.palette}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">{g.style}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Chaos Daemons are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want aggressive, in-your-face melee gameplay</li>
            <li>✓ You love visually wild and horrifying models</li>
            <li>✓ You want a beginner-friendly paint scheme (Khorne)</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy grimdark horror aesthetics</li>
            <li>✓ You want to eventually build a multi-god collection</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want a shooting-focused army (especially Khorne)</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer the Imperium's aesthetic over chaos</li>
            <li>✗ You want psychic powers with Khorne specifically</li>
            <li>✗ You're uncomfortable with the grimdark horror aesthetic</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Khorne Daemons</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Red skin and brass armor — one of the most beginner-friendly schemes in the entire hobby.
        The contrast between deep red and warm brass is dramatic and forgiving of mistakes.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime with Chaos Black or Mephiston Red spray</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Black primer gives you darker, moodier red skin. Mephiston Red spray jumps you straight to the skin base coat. Both work — black gives more depth, red is faster.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base coat skin with Khorne Red</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Cover all the skin areas. Don't worry about getting it on the armor areas — you'll paint those next. The skin is the dominant color and should read as a deep, dark red.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Shade skin with Agrax Earthshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply over all the red skin. It flows into the muscle definition and deepens shadows dramatically. The warm brown of Agrax works beautifully with red — don't use Nuln Oil on red skin.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Layer skin with Wazdakka Red then Evil Sunz Scarlet</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Wazdakka Red on raised muscle areas. Then Evil Sunz Scarlet on the highest points — horns, shoulder muscles, fists. Two quick layers build the red from dark to vibrant.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint armor and weapons: Balthasar Gold → Agrax → Hashut Copper</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Balthasar Gold base on all brass/bronze armor. Agrax Earthshade wash over it (darkens and adds age). Then Hashut Copper on the raised edges to restore the warm metallic shine. This gives an ancient, battle-worn brass look.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Teeth, claws, eyes, and base</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Teeth: Ushabti Bone. Claws: Abaddon Black → drybrush Eshin Grey. Eyes: Yriel Yellow dot. Base: Astrogranite Debris, drybrush Administratum Grey, optional blood effects (Blood for the Blood God technical paint) for Khorne's signature look.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Contrast shortcut -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The Contrast paint shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Prime with <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Grey Seer</strong> or Wraithbone, then apply
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Flesh Tearers Red Contrast</strong> over all skin in one
          coat — it shades and highlights automatically. Then Snakebite Leather Contrast on the
          brass areas. Two Contrast paints, twenty Bloodletters done in an afternoon.
          The results won't be competition level but look genuinely good on a table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. Paint it before buying anything else.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Chaos Daemons</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          All Khorne, all the time. Includes 1x Bloodmaster (Herald of Khorne — your
          character leader), 3x Bloodcrushers (daemon-riders on iron Juggernauts),
          10x Flesh Hounds (fast hunting daemons), and 20x Bloodletters (your core
          melee infantry). 34 models total — one of the most model-rich Combat Patrols available.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The 20 Bloodletters are the backbone. The Flesh Hounds rush forward to tie up
          fast enemy units. The Bloodcrushers are your heavy shock cavalry. The Bloodmaster
          leads from the front and buffs everything around him.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=combat+patrol+chaos+daemons+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon for Combat Patrol →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$45 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Bloodletters (additional 10)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Bloodletters extends your main battleline and gives you flexibility to run larger
          squads or split into two independent units. Khorne lists love redundancy — having
          more foot soldiers means the opponent can't just focus-fire your entire army away.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=bloodletters+of+khorne+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Other gods box -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">If Khorne isn't calling to you...</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Chaos Daemons can be devoted to any of the four Chaos Gods — each plays completely
          differently. You don't have to start with Khorne just because the Combat Patrol is
          Khorne-themed.
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            {
              name: 'Tzeentch Start',
              hint: 'Pink Horrors of Tzeentch box',
              desc: 'The Tzeentch half of the Mortal Realms starter has Pink Horrors — they split into Blue Horrors when killed, making them self-replenishing. Great for psychic-heavy builds.',
              search: 'pink+horrors+tzeentch+warhammer+40k',
            },
            {
              name: 'Nurgle Start',
              hint: 'Plaguebearers of Nurgle box',
              desc: 'Slow but nearly unkillable. Plaguebearers carry disease-ridden blades and are the most durable daemon troops in the game. Excellent for players who prefer attrition.',
              search: 'plaguebearers+nurgle+warhammer+40k',
            },
            {
              name: 'Slaanesh Start',
              hint: 'Daemonettes of Slaanesh box',
              desc: 'Lightning-fast melee. Daemonettes have rending claws and exceptional movement — they get into combat faster than any other daemon troop. High skill ceiling.',
              search: 'daemonettes+slaanesh+warhammer+40k',
            },
          ].map(g => (
            <div class="bg-[#111113] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
              <h4 class="font-display font-semibold mb-1">{g.name}</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mb-2">{g.hint}</p>
              <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-3">{g.desc}</p>
              <a
                href={`https://www.amazon.com/s?k=${g.search}&tag=grimdarkprime-20`}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class="text-[#c9a84c] hover:text-[#dfc070] text-xs font-semibold transition-colors font-display"
              >
                Search Amazon →
              </a>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Khorne)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Khorne Red', use: 'Skin base coat — the foundation', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Shade wash on skin and brass both', required: true },
            { name: 'Wazdakka Red + Evil Sunz Scarlet', use: 'Layer skin from mid to highlight', required: true },
            { name: 'Balthasar Gold', use: 'Brass/bronze armor base', required: true },
            { name: 'Hashut Copper', use: 'Brass armor edge highlight', required: true },
            { name: 'Abaddon Black', use: 'Claws, Hellblade details, hooves', required: true },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone', use: 'Teeth and horns', required: false },
            { name: 'Blood for the Blood God', use: 'Technical paint — splash gore effects', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">The Contrast route (Flesh Tearers Red + Snakebite Leather) requires only Grey Seer spray and two Contrast pots. Much cheaper and still table-ready.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Chaos Daemons', cost: '~$160', note: '34 Khorne models — exceptional model count for the price' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$35', note: 'Reds, shade, brass, black' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey drybrush' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Or plastic glue — both work' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$232</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
